From 52c3f77a428d43a4458557fd735d94012cb91768 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:41:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add MapBiomas Colombia & Pan-Amazon initiatives and WDPA
 (v1.8.1)

Introduce an `initiative` concept so species outside Brazil can be
screened with the same no-GEE workflow:

* brazil   - Collection 10 (1985-2024)  [default, unchanged]
* amazonia - Pan-Amazon / RAISG Collection 6 (1986-2023)
* colombia - Collection 3 (1985-2024)

All three stream per-year Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs from the public
MapBiomas bucket via GDAL /vsicurl/ (no Google Earth Engine, no Google
Drive). Colombia is served per-year on the same bucket
(initiatives/colombia/collection_3/coverage/), so it reads exactly like
Brazil rather than through the multi-band Drive archive.

* New `mb_initiatives()`; `initiative` threaded through `mb_source_url()`,
  `mb_raster_local()`, `mb_years()`, `mb_legend()`, `mb_groups()`,
  `mb_palette()`, `summarise_conversion()`, `cover_timeseries()`,
  `timeseries_for_species()`, `assess_species()`, the map overlay, static
  map, report and Shiny app. `year`/`collection` default to the
  initiative's latest year and native collection.
* `mb_legend()` becomes a single standardised pan-MapBiomas legend built
  from the cross-product harmonisation table (adds codes 81/82 Andinean,
  34 Glacier, 68 Other natural non-vegetated, 74 Banana). Existing Brazil
  codes, names, colours and groups are unchanged.
* Global protected areas: new `wdpa_areas()` / `wdpa_query_url()` read the
  WDPA ArcGIS FeatureServer (bbox query, GeoJSON, cached), standardised to
  the ICMBio pa_name/pa_category/pa_group columns with IUCN categories
  mapped to strict/sustainable groups. `assess_species(pa_source=)`
  defaults to ICMBio for Brazil and WDPA otherwise.
* Assessment summary gains `mapbiomas_initiative`; settings record
  `initiative` and `pa_source`. MapBiomas Fire stays Brazil-only and is
  skipped with a warning for the other initiatives.
* Docs, NEWS, README, DESCRIPTION, man pages, metadata bumped to 1.8.1;
  new tests in test-initiatives.R.

